    Refresh the stated closure rule on every reconcile
    
    An open case whose signal is still present kept the closure_rule recorded at
    creation, so live state kept advertising the removed two-probe rule. State the
    current evidence-and-Judiciary-verification rule whenever the case is touched;
    behaviour stays open and non-closing. Extend the smoke fixture to seed the old
    rule text and assert the refresh.

diff --git a/government/institutional-cases.py b/government/institutional-cases.py
index 5d6166b8..170995d6 100644
--- a/government/institutional-cases.py
+++ b/government/institutional-cases.py
@@ -121,6 +121,9 @@ def reconcile():
             case["last_seen"] = now
             case["observations"] = case.get("observations", 0) + 1
             case["clear_observations"] = 0
+            # Refresh the stated rule on every reconcile. A case created under
+            # the removed two-probe rule must not keep advertising it.
+            case["closure_rule"] = "requires independent Judiciary verification of an evidence-backed investigation"
         elif case.get("state") == "open":
             # Signal absence is observational data, NEVER a recovery verdict.
             # Keep the obligation visible for an Executive investigation and
